```text
Approved as to
form only:
Date:_lit
LEASE
This Lease is made this
______
day of
, 201$, between the City
of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation organized under the laws of the State of Wyoming, 2101
O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 820U1 (“City”), and Little America Hotels & Resorts, Inc.,
a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of Wyoming, 2800 West
Lincoinway, Cheyenne, Wyoming $2001 (“Lessee”).
SECTION ONE
DESCRIPTION OF PROPERTY; TERM
In consideration of the rent provided for in Section Two of this Lease, City leases to
Lessee real property belonging to City located in Laramie County, Wyoming, and more
particularly described as a site for the placement of a billboard advertising sign at a location near
mile post 347.3 on the south side of Interstate 20, approximately 13 miles west of Cheyenne,
Wyoming, for a term of five (5) years beginning on the date that this Lease is fully executed by
the parties. That date shall be hereinafter referred to as the “commencement date.” The
advertising sign site is hereinafter referred to as the “leased property.”
SECTION TWO
RENT
Lessee shall pay City an annual rent of One Thousand ($1,000.00) payable within thirty
(30) days after the commencement date, and payable in the advance on the commencement date
in each year thereafter for the entire term of this Lease.
SECTION THREE
USE OF PROPERTY
Lessee shall use the leased property for the construction and maintenance of a billboard,
measuring no more than 48 feet in length by 14 feet in height, and for no other purpose
whatsoever. Lessee shall not place on the leased property any advertisement for alcohol or
tobacco products.
SENTION FOUR
COMPLIANCE WITH LAW
In its use of the leased property, Lessee shall fully comply with all applicable federal,
state, county and municipal statutes, rules, regulations, and ordinances. In its use of the leased
property, Lessee shall secure from the proper authorities all required licenses and permits before
commencing any construction, re-construction, or significant repair of the billboard.
SECTION FIVE
REPAIRS AND MAINTENANCE
Lessee shall, at all times during the term of this Lease, keep all improvements placed by
Lessee on the leased property in good repair, and shall maintain them at all times in a clean and
attractive condition. Construction and maintenance activities shall be conducted in a manner that
is not hazardous to livestock, including the installation of fencing if necessary to prevent
unreasonable risk ofharm to livestock. Lessee shall be responsible for any and all livestock
injuries and deaths caused or in any way resulting from construction or maintenance activities.
1
