### Page 2 of 5

```text
SECTION SIX
INSURANCE
Lessee shall obtain, and keep in full force and effect at all times during the term of this
Lease, the following specified insurance coverages for the protection of City and Lessee against
liability arising out of the condition of the leased property, the improvements erected on the
property, or any operations of Lessee conducted pursuant to this Lease. In the event the Lessee
retains independent contractors to perform any operations on City land pursuant to this Lease,
the insurance requirements stated in this Section shall also apply to each and every such
contractor.
Commercial General Liabifity Insurance
For claims arising out ofbodily injury, illness or death, or from damage to or destruction
ofproperty of others, including loss or use thereof, with minimum limits of $1,000,000.00 per
occurrence, $2,000,000.00 aggregate for the entire term ofthis Lease.
Business Automobile Insurance
Including owned, non-owned and hired vehicles with minimum limits for bodily injury
and property damage of $1,000,000.00 per accident for the entire term of this Lease.
Workers’ Compensation
Workers’ Compensation coverage shall be in effect for the entire term of the Lease, as
required by Wyoming law, for all employees or agents providing services under this Lease.
Lessee shall provide the City with proof of workers’ compensation or employer’s liability
insurance coverage.
Workers’ Compensation
Statutory
OR
Employer’s Liability
$500,000 Each Accident
$500,000 Each Disease Policy Limit
$500,000 Disease/Each Employee
Additional Insurance Information
Lessee shall provide the City copies of certificates of insurance acknowledging the
above-stated coverages prior to entering upon City’s land for the purpose of conducting any
operations pursuant to this Lease.
It is understood and agreed that these policies are primary and not contributory. All
policies required under this Lease shall be in effect for the duration ofthis Lease. It shall be an
affirmative obligation upon Lessee to immediately notify the City’s Risk Manager, City Clerk
and City Attorney of any fact, circumstance, or occurrence that has resulted in or may result in
the cancellation or substantive change of any insurance coverage required by this Lease, and
failure to do so shall be construed to be a breach of this Lease.
In addition, Lessee shall provide the City with copies of insurance policies and policy
endorsement listing the City of Cheyenne as an additional insured. The City’s failure to request
or review such policies, endorsements, or certificates shall not affect the City’s rights or Lessee’s
obligations hereunder.
Any insurance company providing coverage under this Lease shall have a minimum A.
M. Best rating of A
— (excellent).
