### Page 3 of 5

```text
SECTION SEVEN
OWNERSHIP OF IMPROVEMENTS
All improvements erected by Lessee on the leased property shall remain the property of
Lessee, and shall be removed by Lessee at the termination of this Lease.
SECTION EIGHT
ACCESS TO LEASED PROPERTY
City grants Lessee the right to pass to and from the leased property over City’s private
roads located on the City’s Belvoir Ranch for the purposes of construction, maintenance, and
repair of the billboard advertising sign located on the leased premises; provided, however, that
Lessee shall use said private roads in accordance with good management practices and shall take
reasonable precautions to prevent damage to said roads and to the ranch lands adjacent to said
roads on the leased property.
SECTION NINE
TERMINATION
A.
By City.
1.
If the City should make a bona fide contract for the sale ofthe leased
property, the City may, at City’s option, terminate this Lease by giving Lessee one
hundred and eighty (180) days’ notice in writing, and refunding the Lessee the rental paid
in advance pro rata for the unexpired term of this Lease.
2.
If Lessee defaults in the payment ofrent, or breaches any other covenant
or condition ofthis Lease, the City may, in addition to any other remedy that the City
may have, declare a forfeiture of this Lease for the default, re-enter the leased property,
and remove all personal property from the premises.
B.
By Lessee. During the term ofthis Lease, should the use of the leased property
for the purpose permitted by this Lease be prohibited, limited or restricted by the terms of
any restriction, covenant, regulation, ordinance, or zoning resolution affecting the
property, Lessee may, at Lessee’s option, terminate this Lease by giving the City thirty
(30) days notice in writing of its election to do so.
C.
Upon termination ofthis Lease, Lessee shall restore the leased property to its
natural state including, without limitation, filling all holes and removing all debris caused
by the removal ofbillboard signs and other items of personal property placed on the
leased property by Lessee.
SECTION TEN
EFFECT OF CONDEMNATION
If the leased property, or any part ofthe leased property, is taken by eminent
domain, this Lease shall terminate m the date when title vests pursuant to such taking.
3
```

### Page 4 of 5

```text
SECTION ELEVEN
RENEWAL OPTION
The Lessee Shall have the option to extend this Lease for one additional five (5) year
period, provided, however, that said option may be exercised only if (1) the Lessee is not in
default of any of the terms and conditions of this Lease at the time the option is exercised; (2) the
Lessee has practiced good stewardship of the leased property, access roads, and adjacent ranch
lands as determined by the City in the exercise of its reasonable discretion; and (3) the Lessee
provides written notice to the City of its intent to exercise its option to renew at least one
hundred and twenty-days (120) prior to the scheduled expiration ofthe Lease. Any such
extension shall be on the same terms and conditions as set forth in this Lease, unless such terms
and conditions are amended or renegotiated pursuant to mutual written agreement.
SECTION TWELVE
IDEMNITY
The Lessee agrees to defend, hold harmless, and indemnify the City of Cheyenne, its
officials, employees, agents, and authorized volunteers against and all claims and costs,
including attorney’s fees, arising during or resulting from Lessee’s performance of its obligations
under this Lease. The Lessee acknowledges its understanding of this paragraph and realizes it
may have a financial responsibility to the City. The City does not waive any applicable defenses
and expressly reserves the right to invoke governmental immunity pursuant to the Wyoming
Governmental Claims Act, Wyo. Stat. 1-39-101, et seq. for any claim arising out of this Lease.
It is expressly understood and agre’d that although the City has the right to observe and
review the work and operations of the Lessee, this shall not relieve the Lessee from any of its
covenants and obligations hereunder, and the Lessee shall be responsible for and hold the City
and its officers, employees, agents, and representatives harmless from all suits, actions or claims
of any character due to injuries or damages sustained by any person or property in consequence
of any breach or of default under this Lease, or of failure to observe safety standards or
regulations, or otherwise, or through the use of unsafe ofunacceptable practices or materials in
the performance of any operations under this Lease, of the Lessee’s failure to comply with any
law, ordinance, or regulation.
The parties have executed this Lease the day and year first
above written.
(The remainder of this page left intentionally blank)
4
```

